    brief: "The input has one integer N (1 to 1000000000). Write every number from 1 to N in binary and count how many 1s appear in total. Print that total. N can be as large as 100 crore, so counting the bits of each number one by one will be too slow. The answer can be bigger than a normal int, so use a long type.",
    hint: "Look at one bit position at a time. In the last bit position the pattern is 0,1,0,1,... ; in the next one it is 0,0,1,1,... and so on. For bit position i the pattern repeats every 2^(i+1) numbers with 2^i ones in each block, so count the full blocks and then the leftover part.",
    examples: [{"input":"3","output":"4","explain":"1 is 1, 2 is 10, 3 is 11, so the number of 1s is 1+1+2 = 4."},{"input":"7","output":"12","explain":"The 1s in 1,10,11,100,101,110,111 add up to 1+1+2+1+2+2+3 = 12."}],
    tests: [{"input":"3","output":"4"},{"input":"1","output":"1"},{"input":"7","output":"12"},{"input":"16","output":"33"},{"input":"1000000000","output":"14846928141"}],
    starter: {"python":"n = int(input())\ntotal = 0\n\n# Write your code here. Put the answer in total.\n\nprint(total)\n","javascript":"const data = require('fs').readFileSync(0, 'utf8').trim();\nconst n = Number(data);\nlet total = 0;\n\n// Write your code here. Put the answer in total.\n\nconsole.log(total);\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    long long total = 0;\n\n    // Write your code here. Put the answer in total.\n\n    cout << total << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n","c":"#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main() {\n    long long n;\n    scanf(\"%lld\", &n);\n    long long total = 0;\n\n    /* Write your code here. Put the answer in total. */\n\n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", total);\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.Scanner;\n\nclass Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n        long total = 0;\n\n        // Write your code here. Put the answer in total.\n\n        System.out.println(total);\n    }\n}\n"},
    solution: "n = int(input())\ntotal = 0\ni = 0\nwhile (1 << i) <= n:\n    half = 1 << i\n    block = half * 2\n    total += ((n + 1) // block) * half\n    rem = (n + 1) % block - half\n    if rem > 0:\n        total += rem\n    i += 1\nprint(total)\n",
